Article 2 These Provisions shall apply to the import of personal articles by resident personnel (hereinafter referred to as "resident personnel"), including foreign citizens, overseas Chinese, and residents of Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan (including their cohabiting spouses and minor children) who have been approved to enter China and reside therein for more than one year, and who work for resident offices (hereinafter referred to as "resident offices") established within the territory of China by overseas enterprises, news agencies, economic and trade institutions, cultural groups, and overseas legal persons that have been approved by the competent authorities of the People's Republic of China. Such personnel shall specifically include:
(1) Resident personnel of resident offices in China established by foreign enterprises and other economic, trade, and cultural organizations;
(2) Resident personnel of resident offices in China established by foreign non-governmental economic, trade, and cultural groups;
(3) Resident correspondents of foreign news agencies permanently stationed in China;
(4) Foreign resident personnel of Sino-foreign equity joint ventures, contractual joint ventures, and wholly foreign-owned enterprises in China;
(5) Foreign experts (including experts from Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan) and overseas Chinese experts who have come to China for long-term work;
(6) Foreign students and overseas Chinese students who have come to China for long-term study.
